An elevated twist on classic pumpkin pie from Epicurious. Pure pumpkin purée is spiced with cinnamon, ginger, nutmeg, and cloves, then blended with a rich, from-scratch deep amber caramel cream before baking in a crisp blind-baked crust.

*Adapted from [Epicurious](http://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/caramel-pumpkin-pie-236428).*

## Ingredients

### Crust
- 1 standard round pie dough (homemade or store-bought)
- Pie weights or dried beans (for blind baking)

### Caramel Custard Filling
- 1 cup granulated sugar
- ⅓ cup water
- 2 cups heavy cream, divided
- 1 can (15 oz) solid-pack pure pumpkin purée (not pumpkin pie mix)
- 1 ¼ teaspoons ground ginger
- 1 ¼ teaspoons ground cinnamon
- ¼ teaspoon freshly grated nutmeg
- Pinch of ground cloves
- Scant ½ teaspoon salt
- 4 large eggs, lightly beaten

### Serving
- Lightly sweetened freshly whipped cream

## Instructions

1. **Fit and Chill the Dough:** Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C) with the rack placed in the center. On a lightly floured surface, roll out the pie dough into a 14-inch round. Fit it gently into a 10-inch fluted metal quiche pan with a removable bottom (or a 9- to 10-inch deep-dish pie plate), trimming excess dough flush with the rim. Chill in the refrigerator for 30 minutes until firm.
2. **Blind-Bake the Shell:** Lightly prick the bottom of the chilled shell all over with a fork. Line with aluminum foil and fill to the brim with pie weights or dried beans. Set the pan on a baking sheet and bake for 18 to 20 minutes until the sides are set and pale golden. Carefully lift out the foil and weights, then return to the oven for 10 minutes more until the bottom is dry and golden. Cool completely on a wire rack.
3. **Make the Caramel Cream:** In a heavy 3-quart saucepan, combine the sugar and water over medium-high heat, stirring just until the sugar dissolves. Bring to a boil and cook without stirring, occasionally brushing down the sides of the pan with a wet pastry brush and swirling the pan gently, for about 10 minutes until the syrup becomes a deep golden amber caramel. Reduce heat to medium and carefully pour in 1 cup of the heavy cream (it will foam vigorously). Stir until the caramel dissolves into the cream, then stir in the remaining 1 cup of cream and bring just to a gentle simmer. Remove from heat.
4. **Mix the Filling:** In a large bowl, whisk together the pumpkin purée, ginger, cinnamon, nutmeg, cloves, and salt. Slowly stream in the warm caramel cream while whisking continuously. Add the beaten eggs, whisking until thoroughly combined and glossy.
5. **Bake the Pie:** Pour the pumpkin filling into the cooled crust. Bake at 375°F for 55 to 60 minutes, until the filling is puffed about 1 ½ inches from the outer rim and the center is just set with a gentle jiggle.
6. **Cool and Serve:** Transfer to a wire rack and cool completely in the pan for at least 2 hours (the pie will continue setting as it comes to room temperature). Remove the outer ring of the pan, slice into wedges, and serve with dollops of whipped cream.

## Notes

- **Caramel Tip:** Watch the sugar closely in the final minutes—it transitions quickly from golden amber to burnt. As soon as it reaches deep amber, reduce heat and add the cream immediately.
- **Deep Dish:** Using a 10-inch fluted tart or quiche pan with a removable bottom yields clean, beautiful fluted slices.
